! BINARY VFL ADD AND LOAD: RN ON A NEGATIVE ZERO, LOST CARRY, PARTIAL
! FIELD -- docs/NEXT.md's G2.3 findings 1 and 2, settled 2026-11-16.
!
! Every expected value below is HAND-DERIVED from the Reference Manual
! 22-6530-2 (printed N = PDF N+3), read in the page images; none was taken
! from a run.  The capture is vfl_decimal_add.strap's: Z, $IND before the
! operation, the indicator register copied with TI (count one) to Ik
! after it, then the accumulator words 8, 9, 10 ($L, $R, $SB) stored to
! Xk, Xk+1, Xk+2.  Indicator word bits (bit n is 1 << (63-n)): LC
! 0x20000000000, PF 0x10000000000, RLZ 0x80, RZ 0x40, RGZ 0x20, RN 0x10.
! The sign byte register's sign bit is IBM bit 4 of word 10:
! 0x0800000000000000.  A signed binary field at byte size 8 ends in an
! eight-bit sign byte whose sign bit is the byte's bit 4 (0x08), as in
! plus_mg.strap's NEG5.
!
! THE RULES:
!  RN  printed p.47 (PDF 50), indicator 59: "Result Negative (RN).  The
!      result of the non-comparative arithmetic operation just executed
!      was negative whether zero or not.  This indicator is turned off by
!      a non-comparative arithmetic operation whose result is positive,
!      whether zero or not".  No radix in it; printed p.60's ADD example
!      4 (decimal) shows it: "00000-  Result zero  Result negative".
!      printed p.60 also fixes the sign of a zero sum: "On any operation
!      in which the result in the accumulator is all zero, the sign
!      remains as it was before the operation began."
!  LC  printed p.60, ADD: "This indicator is actuated if information is
!      lost because a carry attempts to propagate beyond the left end of
!      the accumulator"; printed p.59: "In to-accumulator operations, this
!      indicator is turned on when a carry attempts to propagate beyond
!      the left end of the accumulator."
!  PF  printed p.60: "turned on if significant bits of the data field from
!      storage overlap the left end of the accumulator.  The accumulator
!      operand is extended with high-order zeros to combine with the
!      storage operand, but the high-order bits of the result are
!      dropped.  A partial field condition will not cause a lost carry
!      indication.  However, both conditions may arise during the
!      execution of a single instruction."
!  +MG printed p.61: "Lost Carry (LC); Partial Field (PF); ...
!      Arithmetic Result (RLZ, RZ, RGZ, RN).  These indicators are set as
!      in ADD."  printed p.60: "If the result is negative, the entire
!      accumulator is cleared to zero.  In either case, the content of the
!      accumulator sign byte register is not changed."
!  L   printed p.61: "Partial Field (PF); ... Arithmetic Result (RLZ, RZ,
!      RGZ, RN).  These indicators are set as in ADD."  "The sign bit in
!      the sign byte register is set according to the sign of the data".
!
! THE CASES (the old model's value, where it differs, in brackets):
!  B1  + : acc -5 (L of N5), + (BU,8,8) 5: unlike signs, |acc| = |op|,
!          the sign "remains as it was": 0-.  RZ RN 0x50.         [0x40]
!  B2  + : acc +5, + (B,16,8) -5: 0+.  RZ 0x40.  CONTROL: a positive zero
!          keeps RN off.
!  B3  +MG: acc -5, +MG (B,16,8) -7: |-5| + -7 = -2, negative, the whole
!          accumulator cleared, the sign byte kept (minus): 0-.  RZ RN
!          0x50 -- the binary twin of vfl_decimal_add's A10.        [0x40]
!  B4  L : (B,16,8) numeric 0, sign minus: 0-.  RZ RN 0x50.      [0x40]
!  B5  LC: acc 128 ones, + (BU,8,8) 1 at offset 0: the carry leaves the
!          left end; acc 0, positive.  LC RZ 0x20000000040.        [0x40]
!  B6  PF: acc (16)12, + (BU,16,8) (16)9876 at offset 120: bits 120-135,
!          (16)98 past the left end, (16)76 lands in bits 120-127.  accL
!          (16)7600000000000000, accR (16)12.  PF RGZ 0x10000000020. [0x20]
!  B7  PF, no LC: acc 0, + (16)0100 at offset 120: the 1 is dropped, 0
!          lands; result 0.  PF RZ, LC off: 0x10000000040.        [0x40]
!  B8  PF and LC together: acc 128 ones, + (16)0101 at offset 120: (16)01
!          dropped (PF), (16)01 at bit 120 carries out (LC); acc 2^120 - 1:
!          accL (16)00FFFFFFFFFFFFFF, accR all ones.  LC PF RGZ
!          0x30000000020.                                         [0x20]
!  B9  +MG, LC and RN at once: acc -(2^128 - 1) (L of -1, then - (BU,64,8)
!          ones at offset 64 and - (2^64 - 2) at 0), +MG (BU,8,8) 1:
!          |acc| + 1 = 2^128, positive, the carry lost; acc 0 with the sign
!          byte unchanged (minus).  LC RZ RN 0x20000000050.        [0x40]
!  B10 + : acc 128 ones, + (B,16,8) -1: unlike signs never carry.
!          acc 2^128 - 2.  RGZ 0x20.  CONTROL.
!  B11 L PF: (BU,16,8) (16)9876 at offset 120: accL (16)7600000000000000,
!          accR 0.  PF RGZ 0x10000000020.                         [0x20]
!  B12 L : the same field at offset 112, in range: accL
!          (16)9876000000000000.  RGZ 0x20.  CONTROL.
!
! MEASURED 2026-11-16.  The UNMODIFIED model (batch9) FAILS B1, B3, B4
! (0x40), B5 (0x40), B6 (0x20), B7 (0x40), B8 (0x20), B9 (0x40), B11 (0x20)
! -- exactly the bracketed values -- and passes B2, B10, B12 and every
! accumulator and sign byte check.  INJECTIONS into the fixed model, each
! run on this deck, vfl_decimal_add and vfl_progressive_refill_once, each
! in its own scratch copy of the tree (the worktree never held one):
!   i1 RN back to "sign && !zero" in setResultIndicatorsF: FAILS B1, B3, B4
!      (0x40), B9 (0x20000000040), and vfl_decimal_add's A4_ind_RZ_RN,
!      A10_ind, M8_ind -- the decimal and binary arms share the rule.
!   i2 binary + never sets LC: FAILS B5 (0x40), B8 (0x10000000020), B9
!      (0x50).
!   i3 binary + never sets PF: FAILS B6 (0x20), B7 (0x40), B8
!      (0x20000000020).
!   i4 LC without the like-sign test: FAILS B10 (0x20000000020) only.
!   i5 LC from the WIDE operand (a partial field allowed to carry): FAILS
!      B7 (0x30000000040, LC from a dropped bit) and B8 (0x10000000020).
!   i6 binary L never sets PF: FAILS B11 (0x20) only.
! The other two decks stayed green under i2-i6.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   L(B,16,8), N5
        Z, $IND
        +(BU,8,8), FIVE
        TI, 1, $IND, I1
        ST(BU,64,8), X1, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X1+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X1+2.0
        L(BU,8,8), FIVE
        Z, $IND
        +(B,16,8), N5
        TI, 1, $IND, I2
        ST(BU,64,8), X2, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X2+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X2+2.0
        L(B,16,8), N5
        Z, $IND
        +MG(B,16,8), N7
        TI, 1, $IND, I3
        ST(BU,64,8), X3, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X3+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X3+2.0
        Z, $IND
        L(B,16,8), NZ
        TI, 1, $IND, I4
        ST(BU,64,8), X4, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X4+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X4+2.0
        L(BU,64,8), ONES, 64
        +(BU,64,8), ONES, 0
        Z, $IND
        +(BU,8,8), ONE
        TI, 1, $IND, I5
        ST(BU,64,8), X5, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X5+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X5+2.0
        L(BU,8,8), D12
        Z, $IND
        +(BU,16,8), H9876, 120
        TI, 1, $IND, I6
        ST(BU,64,8), X6, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X6+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X6+2.0
        L(BU,8,8), ZERO
        Z, $IND
        +(BU,16,8), H0100, 120
        TI, 1, $IND, I7
        ST(BU,64,8), X7, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X7+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X7+2.0
        L(BU,64,8), ONES, 64
        +(BU,64,8), ONES, 0
        Z, $IND
        +(BU,16,8), H0101, 120
        TI, 1, $IND, I8
        ST(BU,64,8), X8, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X8+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X8+2.0
        L(B,16,8), N1
        -(BU,64,8), ONES, 64
        -(BU,64,8), ONESM1, 0
        Z, $IND
        +MG(BU,8,8), ONE
        TI, 1, $IND, I9
        ST(BU,64,8), X9, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X9+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X9+2.0
        L(BU,64,8), ONES, 64
        +(BU,64,8), ONES, 0
        Z, $IND
        +(B,16,8), N1
        TI, 1, $IND, I10
        ST(BU,64,8), X10, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X10+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X10+2.0
        Z, $IND
        L(BU,16,8), H9876, 120
        TI, 1, $IND, I11
        ST(BU,64,8), X11, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X11+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X11+2.0
        Z, $IND
        L(BU,16,8), H9876, 112
        TI, 1, $IND, I12
        ST(BU,64,8), X12, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), X12+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), X12+2.0
PASS    BEW, $


        SLC, 1500.0
N5      DD(BU,64), (16)0508000000000000
N7      DD(BU,64), (16)0708000000000000
NZ      DD(BU,64), (16)0008000000000000
N1      DD(BU,64), (16)0108000000000000
ONE     DD(BU,64), (16)0100000000000000
FIVE    DD(BU,64), (16)0500000000000000
